# Web Development Fundamentals

Before you can learn React, Django, or Node.js, you must master the "Big Three" of the web: HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.

## 🎯 Core Concepts to Master
- **HTML**: Semantic tags, Forms, Accessibility (a11y).
- **CSS**: Flexbox, CSS Grid, Responsive Design (Media Queries).
- **JavaScript**: DOM manipulation, Fetch API, ES6 (Promises, Arrow Functions).

## 📚 The Golden Path (Free Resources)
1. **[The Odin Project](https://www.theodinproject.com/)**: The best free, open-source full-stack curriculum in the world. Start with their "Foundations" course.
2. **[MDN Web Docs](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/)**: The official documentation for the web. Use this as your reference manual.
3. **[Frontend Mentor](https://www.frontendmentor.io/)**: Download professional designs and try to build them yourself to practice your CSS.

